## Your job

Decide whether this continuity claim is `plausible` or `implausible`.
A claim is plausible if the two findings are genuinely about the same
underlying code location/topic/concern — not merely the same file, not
merely superficially similar wording. Do not defer to the claiming
agent's rationale being confidently worded; assess the file/line/
description content yourself, independently.

Importantly, "continues" includes the case where the flagged location
was edited in direct response to the prior finding, and this round's
finding is about a NEW problem introduced by that very edit. That is
still the same underlying concern evolving across rounds, not two
unrelated problems — do not judge a claim implausible just because the
specific complaint changed between rounds, if both rounds are about the
same code doing the same job. Reserve `implausible` for claims where the
two findings are actually about different code locations, different
jobs, or different topics entirely.

